Z||000000||sjp777||05-20-2001||01:54 AM||||I've been looking at late model Grand AMs lately and I've noticed their mirrors are painted to match body, have a really nice design and they mount on that triangle piece that is remarkably similar in size and shape to the Fiero piece.<P>Anybody try to retro-fit them on the Fiero?<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||05-20-2001||07:50 AM||||Speaking of being painted, I did the same to my wife's Fiero and it looks great!<BR>It really turns peoples heads when they try to figure out what it is...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||05-20-2001||11:45 AM||||Dude,those mirrors would be HUGE on a Fiero!  Don't know if the look would work or not....  But since I have a Fiero, and a 99 Grand Am, maybe I need to check into this...||||reg||6
