Z||000005||Formula88||05-21-2001||09:34 AM||||One other note: the Grand Am mirrors are only painted body color on the GT's.  The SE's have the black mirrors. (Mine in an SE).<P>Hell, I'm still trying to figure out how to swap the 3400SFI from my GA into the Fiero!  It's rated at 175Hp (185 in the Asstek) with room for improvement.  It's a very smooth engine, with almost all of it's torque from off-idle throughout the rev-range.  Very flat torque curve.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mr.Frosty||05-21-2001||12:47 PM||||I've been thinking along those lines and agree that they're too big,BUT on the other hand I'm looking at the new Bonneville mirrors.Same size as Fiero and they're more modern and nice looking.You can also get them with the blue tinted glass for glare reduction....sweeet.They have a similar size triangular base that would surely mount on the fiero,if not with a little modification.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-Sold <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||10
Z||000007||286SE'S||05-21-2001||03:32 PM||||This has been discussed before. You cannot put the mirrors there. The door glass will hit them. DUH.<BR>(Yes, WHEN you open the door)<p>[This message has been edited by 286SE'S (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||05-21-2001||03:59 PM||||Originally posted by 286SE'S:<BR>"This has been discussed before. You cannot put the mirrors there. The door glass will hit them. DUH."<P>&gt;Yep, I've said it before.  I was going to make a kit for them, but I concluded that the maximum width could only be 3-4" w/o getting in the way of the window glass when it arcs.  The reason they work on the GAs is probably because the mirror comes along with the door when you open it.  I'm not sure though.  The only way it would work is if you found a way to mount the triangular piece onto the door.  I think....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||3
Z||000009||rockcrawl||05-21-2001||04:00 PM||||You need to remove the black plastic triangular trim piece from the Fiero and fabricate a triagular steel plate to be welded to the Fiero door frame. That way the mirror will swing out with the door.||||reg||1
